WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.340
In the sea, a jellyfish keeps its shape.

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.710
Lift it out onto the
sand, and it collapses.

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.980
Touch a hydra gently, and
its whole body shortens.

4
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.900
An earthworm moves through soil
by getting longer and shorter,

5
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.540
again and again.

6
00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.080
There is no bone anywhere in it.

7
00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.270
So with no bones, what
holds each one in shape?

8
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:28.090
In this mission, you'll learn three
questions that place any animal in its group:

9
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.600
its symmetry, its gut, and its support.

10
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.590
Then you'll look inside a hydra,
a flatworm and an earthworm,

11
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.010
and compare them.

12
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: find out what holds each
of these boneless bodies in shape.
